#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/btree.rst:12
#: 91a9839157f843f3979f8443dc7d60f3
msgid ""
"A **B-Tree** is a self-balancing search tree optimized for systems that "
"read and write large blocks of data. Unlike binary trees where each node "
"has at most 2 children, B-Tree nodes can have many children, reducing "
"tree height and minimizing disk I/O operations. B-Trees are the "
"fundamental data structure behind modern database systems and file "
"systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/btree.rst:40
#: 538948462d934fc8ae7862c81e658876
msgid ""
"B-Trees are ideal for storage systems where reading/writing a block of "
"data has similar cost regardless of block size. By storing multiple keys "
"per node, B-Trees minimize the number of disk accesses required for "
"operations."
msgstr ""

